## Code Review: Runtime Metrics Exposure

### Root Cause

The `MetricsTracker` class in `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/metrics.ts` correctly tracks runtime metrics, but **these metrics are never exposed to clients** via the WebSocket protocol. They're only:
1. Persisted to disk in `persistSession()`
2. Logged to `logs/runtime-metrics.jsonl`

The protocol in `packages/protocol/src/messages.ts` has no `metrics` field in any server message type.

---

### Smallest Protocol-First Change Set

#### 1. **`packages/protocol/src/messages.ts`** — Add metrics to `session.state` payload

```typescript
export type ServerMessage =
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "session.state";
      payload: {
        phase: SessionPhase;
        paused: boolean;
        preparedSeed: number | null;
        threadIds: { gameplayByAgentId: Record<string, string>; builder?: string };
        connected: boolean;
        runtime: {
          model: string | null;
          effort: TurnEffort;
          tickMs: number;
          schedulerMs: number;
          maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn: number;
          availableModels: RuntimeModelOption[];
        };
        metrics?: {
          turnsTotal: number;
          invalidOutputCount: number;
          actionAppliedCount: number;
          actionRejectedCount: number;
          queuedActions: number;
        };
      };
    }
```

#### 2. **`apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts`** — Include metrics in `sendSessionState()`

Find `sendSessionState()` and update:

```typescript
private sendSessionState(): void {
  this.emitMessage({
    version: PROTOCOL_VERSION,
    type: "session.state",
    payload: {
      phase: this.phase,
      paused: this.paused,
      preparedSeed: this.preparedSeed,
      threadIds: this.threadIds,
      connected: this.connected,
      runtime: {
        model: this.turnModel,
        effort: this.turnEffort,
        tickMs: runtimeConfig.tickMs,
        schedulerMs: runtimeConfig.schedulerMs,
        maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn: runtimeConfig.maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn,
        availableModels: this.availableModels
      },
      metrics: this.metrics.snapshot()  // ← ADD THIS LINE
    }
  });
}
```

#### 3. **`apps/game-client/src/App.tsx`** — Store and display metrics

Add state:
```typescript
const [metrics, setMetrics] = useState<{
  turnsTotal: number;
  invalidOutputCount: number;
  actionAppliedCount: number;
  actionRejectedCount: number;
  queuedActions: number;
} | null>(null);
```

Update `session.state` handler:
```typescript
case "session.state":
  setPhase(message.payload.phase);
  setPaused(message.payload.paused);
  setPreparedSeed(message.payload.preparedSeed);
  setThreadIds(message.payload.threadIds);
  setRuntimeModel(message.payload.runtime.model);
  setRuntimeEffort(message.payload.runtime.effort);
  setRuntimeSchedulerMs(message.payload.runtime.schedulerMs);
  setRuntimeQueueAhead(message.payload.runtime.maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn);
  setAvailableModels(message.payload.runtime.availableModels);
  setMetrics(message.payload.metrics ?? null);  // ← ADD THIS LINE
  if (message.payload.phase === "idle") {
    setTick(0);
    setRuntimeAgents([]);
    setCatalog({ prefabs: [], recipes: [] });
    sceneRef.current?.clearSnapshot();
  }
  return;
```

Add to topbar display:
```tsx
<span className="pill">Turns: {metrics?.turnsTotal ?? 0}</span>
<span className="pill">Invalid: {metrics?.invalidOutputCount ?? 0}</span>
<span className="pill">Applied: {metrics?.actionAppliedCount ?? 0}</span>
<span className="pill">Rejected: {metrics?.actionRejectedCount ?? 0}</span>
<span className="pill">Queued: {metrics?.queuedActions ?? 0}</span>
```

---

### Regression Checks

| Check | Command/Action |
|-------|---------------|
| Protocol types compile | `cd packages/protocol && tsc --noEmit` |
| Runtime compiles | `cd apps/game-runtime && tsc --noEmit` |
| Client compiles | `cd apps/game-client && tsc --noEmit` |
| Existing tests pass | `npm test` |
| Metrics appear in UI | Start runtime, start session, verify topbar shows metrics |
| Metrics increment correctly | Trigger turns, invalid outputs, actions; verify counters increase |
| Session restore includes metrics | Check `persistSession()` still saves `metrics.snapshot()` |

---

### Why This Is Minimal

1. **No new message types** — reuses existing `session.state`
2. **No new endpoints** — metrics piggyback on existing state updates
3. **No breaking changes** — `metrics` is optional (`metrics?`)
4. **Runtime remains authoritative** — client only reads, doesn't write metrics
5. **Existing persistence unchanged** — `persistSession()` already calls `this.metrics.snapshot()`
